---
import Research from '../../layouts/Research.astro';
import ResearchFigure from '../../islands/ResearchFigure.tsx';
import { analysis, analysisRows } from '../../lib/analysis';
import { cardCount, formatCount } from '../../lib/data';
import { RESEARCH_PAGES } from '../../lib/research-nav';

const t = analysisRows.by_tier;
const single = analysisRows.single_token;
const listed = t['2+ families'] + t['1 family'];
const pct = (n: number, d: number) => `${((100 * n) / d).toFixed(1)}%`;
const alone = analysis<{ by_family: Record<string, number> }>('S4').data.by_family;
const pages = RESEARCH_PAGES.filter((p) => p.slug);
---

<Research
  title="Research"
  slug=""
  description="The CEOL Universe measured: how the published word lists compare over the same strings, the technical report, the literature, and a proposed study."
>
  <header class="page-head">
    <h1>Research</h1>
    <p class="lede">
      What the universe holds, and how the published word lists compare when every list is measured against the same
      strings. Every figure here is computed from version 1.0's files by committed code.
    </p>
  </header>

  <p class="findings">
    Of the {formatCount(single)} single-token rows, <strong>{formatCount(listed)}</strong> ({pct(listed, single)}) are listed by
    at least 1 published list and <strong>{formatCount(t['corpus only'])}</strong> ({pct(t['corpus only'], single)}) rest on
    a corpus alone. Most listed rows are listed by 1 family: <strong>{pct(alone['Wiktionary'], listed)}</strong> of them by
    Wiktionary and no other. <strong>{formatCount(t['2+ families'])}</strong> rows, the consensus core, are listed by 2 or
    more independent families.
  </p>

  <section class="compared" aria-labelledby="compared">
    <h2 id="compared">The sources compared</h2>
    <p class="section-lede">
      No single list can measure this, because none is measured against the others. Each figure counts the single-token
      rows, over the rows each list could hold; a list that cannot hold a class is never counted as not listing it.
    </p>
    <div class="fig-grid">
      <ResearchFigure client:load id="S2" entry={analysis('S2')} />
      <ResearchFigure client:load id="S3" entry={analysis('S3')} />
    </div>
    <ResearchFigure client:load id="S6" entry={analysis('S6')} />
    <div class="fig-grid">
      <ResearchFigure client:load id="S5" entry={analysis('S5')} />
      <ResearchFigure client:load id="S13" entry={analysis('S13')} />
    </div>
    <p class="more">
      The technical report states the method and every figure: <a href="/research/report/#7-the-sources-compared">the
      sources compared</a>.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="pages" aria-labelledby="pages">
    <h2 id="pages">In this section</h2>
    <ul>
      {
        pages.map((p) => (
          <li>
            <a href={`/research/${p.slug}/`}>{p.label}</a>
            <p>{p.blurb}</p>
          </li>
        ))
      }
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="prose open" aria-labelledby="open">
    <h2 id="open">Open questions</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>Parts of speech.</strong> The universe records none; WordNet's listing covers only the rows it lists. A later
        version adds a part-of-speech layer, lemma and inflection relations, and WordNet's categories.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Offensive content.</strong> Its share is not measured. The measure needs an offensive-term lexicon whose
        license allows the use.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Recognition errors.</strong> How many corpus-only rows are errors of scanning would need a labeled sample,
        which this project chose not to make.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>The standard estimators of uncaptured strings.</strong> How far they miss on a closed frame inside the
        universe, where the answer is known, is planned as a calibration, never as a count of missing English strings.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>All {cardCount('panel_set_count')} lists.</strong> The comparison over the withheld lists as well waits for the license review to
        confirm that aggregate counts may be published.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Change over time.</strong> What each source adds and drops between versions needs a second snapshot of
        each.
      </li>
    </ul>
  </section>
</Research>

<style>
  .page-head {
    display: grid;
    gap: var(--space-3);
  }
  .page-head h1 {
    font-size: var(--step-5);
  }
  .findings {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-size: var(--step-2);
    line-height: 1.4;
    max-width: 44rem;
    padding-block: var(--space-4);
    border-block: 1px solid var(--rule);
  }
  .findings strong {
    font-weight: 600;
  }
  .compared {
    display: grid;
    gap: var(--space-6);
  }
  .compared h2,
  .pages h2,
  .open h2 {
    font-size: var(--step-3);
  }
  .section-lede {
    max-width: var(--measure);
    color: var(--ink-soft);
    margin-top: calc(-1 * var(--space-4));
  }
  .fig-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(min(100%, 28rem), 1fr));
    gap: var(--space-7);
    align-items: start;
  }
  .more {
    font-size: var(--step--1);
    color: var(--ink-soft);
  }
  .pages ul {
    list-style: none;
    margin: var(--space-4) 0 0;
    padding: 0;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--rule);
  }
  .pages li {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(11rem, 15rem) 1fr;
    gap: var(--space-2) var(--space-5);
    padding-block: var(--space-3);
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--rule);
    align-items: baseline;
  }
  .pages li a {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-size: var(--step-1);
    font-weight: 600;
    text-decoration: none;
  }
  .pages li p {
    color: var(--ink-soft);
  }
  @media (max-width: 36rem) {
    .pages li {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }
  }
  .open ul {
    padding-left: 1.25rem;
    display: grid;
    gap: var(--space-3);
  }
</style>
